# pneu mailroom

The registry-selected maildir is the delivery fact; the Grok monitor only
starts a turn when that durable inbox changes. On a monitor event, use the
package-managed absolute command paths supplied by the launcher:

- `<pneu-prefix>/bin/rt-inbox --fenced --archive-quiet-acks -f json`
- `<pneu-prefix>/bin/rt-ack --fenced <id>[,<id>...]`
- `<pneu-prefix>/bin/rt-say --fenced --no-nudge <agent> <kind> <message>`

Act on every non-ack message before acknowledging it once. Quiet receipts are
archived by the fenced inbox command and are never acknowledged again.

A bare `rt-grok` launch uses one visible activation turn to create exactly one
`monitor` background task with `persistent: true`. The monitor is scoped to the
native Grok session. After resuming a session, or when the launcher says its
primer was skipped, perform one monitor re-arm turn before relying on automatic
wake; do not create a second monitor in an already armed session.
